<title>ESTONIA: EESTI GAAS AND OLUMPIA SALES TO BE APPROVED.</title>
<headline>EESTI GAAS AND OLUMPIA SALES TO BE APPROVED.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Estonian privatization agency will approve tomorrow the conditions for the sale of minority shares in Eesti Gaas, Hotel Olumpia and metalworking firm Esmeta.</p>
<p>The agency decided earlier to sell a 12.33 percent stake in Eesti Gaas, 25.06 percent stake of Hotel Olumpia and 24 percent of Esmeta. German Ruhrgas and Russian Gazprom already own around 45 percent of Eesti Gaas.</p>
<p>The agency will sell the shares via a public offer for vouchers.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn Newsroom, +372 630 8400, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
